        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12422453/comment/12703173",
          "id": "12703173",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=thomasm",
            "name": "thomasm",
            "key": "tmueller",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Thomas Mueller",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Zurich"
          },
          "body": "I just found out, there is already a class LazyFileInputStream (that does basically the same) in the package org.apache.jackrabbit.util. However this one doesn't close the file after reading the last byte.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=thomasm",
            "name": "thomasm",
            "key": "tmueller",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Thomas Mueller",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Zurich"
          },
          "created": "2009-04-27T15:27:01.397+0000",
          "updated": "2009-04-27T15:27:01.397+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12422453/comment/12708352",
          "id": "12708352",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=akiraly",
            "name": "akiraly",
            "key": "akiraly",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=akiraly&avatarId=10137",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=akiraly&avatarId=10137",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=akiraly&avatarId=10137",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=akiraly&avatarId=10137"
            },
            "displayName": "Attila Kir\u00e1ly",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Budapest"
          },
          "body": "We run into a \"too many open files\" problem with using FileDataStore and adding a massive ammount of data to the repository (around 80GB documents). We were not searching just adding elements to the repository.\n\nHowever using the modifications of this issue (namly /jackrabbit/trunk/jackrabbit-core/src/main/java/org/apache/jackrabbit/core/data/FileDataRecord.java and /jackrabbit/trunk/jackrabbit-core/src/main/java/org/apache/jackrabbit/core/data/LazyFileInputStream.java) solves our issue. Is it possible that this modification gets ported to the 1.5.x branch?\n\nWe tested with 1.5.5 and these two files.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=akiraly",
            "name": "akiraly",
            "key": "akiraly",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=akiraly&avatarId=10137",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=akiraly&avatarId=10137",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=akiraly&avatarId=10137",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=akiraly&avatarId=10137"
            },
            "displayName": "Attila Kir\u00e1ly",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Budapest"
          },
          "created": "2009-05-12T07:30:30.755+0000",
          "updated": "2009-05-12T07:30:30.755+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12422453/comment/12708857",
          "id": "12708857",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=thomasm",
            "name": "thomasm",
            "key": "tmueller",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Thomas Mueller",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Zurich"
          },
          "body": "For me, back-porting to 1.5.5 would be OK.\n\nTo move the LazyFileInputStream to the jackrabbit-jcr-commons package we would need to add a dependency to Apache Commons IO in this project as well:\n \n    <dependency>\n      <groupId>commons-io</groupId>\n      <artifactId>commons-io</artifactId>\n    </dependency>\n",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=thomasm",
            "name": "thomasm",
            "key": "tmueller",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Thomas Mueller",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Zurich"
          },
          "created": "2009-05-13T09:27:51.224+0000",
          "updated": "2009-05-13T09:27:51.224+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12422453/comment/12710800",
          "id": "12710800",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=akiraly",
            "name": "akiraly",
            "key": "akiraly",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=akiraly&avatarId=10137",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=akiraly&avatarId=10137",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=akiraly&avatarId=10137",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=akiraly&avatarId=10137"
            },
            "displayName": "Attila Kir\u00e1ly",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Budapest"
          },
          "body": "I suggest not invoking super.close() in LazyFileInputStream if the stream was never opened because it can result in a NPE (and we got one with Jackrabbit).\n\nSo maybe something like this would be better:\npublic void close() throws IOException {\n  if (!opened)  \n    opened = true;\n  else\n    super.close();\n}",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=akiraly",
            "name": "akiraly",
            "key": "akiraly",
            "avatarUrls": {
